.resources/TASK-260830-2xt6fd/TASK-260830-2xt6fd_resume-rev1.md-2-
.resources/TASK-260830-2xt6fd/TASK-260830-2xt6fd_resume-rev1.md:3:STATE. The Story branch carries two signed checkpoints from 2026-09-07/08: 2bnr39 (git repository and index snapshot, `119d562`) and 3m7m7w (untracked/ignored/symlink/submodule capture, `d73a285`). Both sit on an OLD base, `7654d7c`, 40 trunk commits behind. That range includes the v0.7.0 spec and registry adoption. Your earlier uncommitted work on this leaf (18 paths in `internal/gitsnap` and `internal/provhost`, README, LOGBOOK) is still in `.temp/STORY-260830-35dbcs/worktree`, and so are your attached outcomes and blocked audits. Before touching anything, back up the candidate: stage it into a scratch `GIT_INDEX_FILE`, then `write-tree` + `commit-tree` into `refs/backup/2xt6fd-pre-refresh-<UTC>`.
.resources/TASK-260830-2xt6fd/TASK-260830-2xt6fd_resume-rev1.md-4-
.resources/TASK-260830-2xt6fd/TASK-260830-2xt6fd_resume-rev1.md:5:STEP 1: REFRESH. Run `task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-2xt6fd` onto current trunk (`6d3bff9`, or later if it moved). First combine incoming trunk content into your candidate for every path that both sides changed; the tool requires this. The replay of the two checkpoints will likely conflict on README.md, LOGBOOK.md and any TRACEABILITY/registry file. Resolve through the tool's `--replay-resolutions` template (bound to REBASE_HEAD, path and SHA-256), never by hand-committing. Resolutions are the union of trunk and Story. THE INVARIANT: every trunk-only path in `git diff --name-only 7654d7c <new trunk>` that the Story does not change must be BLOB-EQUAL to the new trunk. Prove it mechanically over the full list; `refresh-candidate` can leave stale copies (task-board #346/#321). If it refuses, record the typed refusal and stop.
